diff --git a/docs/requirements.rst b/docs/requirements.rst
index fede671..f042275 100644
--- a/docs/requirements.rst
+++ b/docs/requirements.rst
@@ -69,6 +69,18 @@ Usage
     not have such rules, and the check incorrectly disallows valid requirement
     strings from being parsed.
 
+Requirements support replacement of individual fields without modifying the
+original. Unspecified fields are kept; replacement values are validated and
+normalized by parsing. Specifiers are copied with their prerelease settings.
+
+.. doctest::
+
+    >>> req = Requirement('requests[security]>=2.0; python_version >= "3"')
+    >>> req.__replace__(name="flask")
+    <Requirement('flask[security]>=2.0; python_version >= "3"')>
+
+On Python 3.13 and later, :func:`copy.replace` also supports requirements.
+
 Reference
 ---------
 
